s the best estimate for the number of trees in the entire orchard?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213675 1072 #uuid "05c9aba7-aa33-50e5-ac63-23bba0318e29" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213675 1073 true 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213676 1068 #edb/ref 17592186211863 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213676 1069 "q-301277" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213676 1071 "A sports analyst wants to estimate the typical number of points scored by a local basketball team in a season. The team has played in $320$ games over the past several years. The analyst randomly selects $7$ of those games and records the points scored: $102$, $96$, $88$, $105$, $99$, $94$, and $110$.\n\nBased on the **median** of the sample, which of the following ranges contains the best estimate for the total number of points scored in all $320$ games?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213676 1072 #uuid "aa4fa5a0-d90b-5b52-b3fb-921ab9808b9b" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213676 1073 true 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213677 1068 #edb/ref 17592186211869 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213677 1069 "q-301294" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213677 1071 "At a coffee shop, $2,400$ customers made purchases last Saturday. The manager randomly reviewed receipts from $80$ customers and found that $12$ of those customers purchased a pastry. Which of the following is the most appropriate conclusion?" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213677 1072 #uuid "75ff780a-2020-5dad-9f40-a190fae405dc" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213678 1068 #edb/ref 17592186211875 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213678 1069 "q-301309" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213678 1071 "At a university, the transportation office wants to estimate the s