h firm surveyed $1,200$ workers who were selected at random from a large metropolitan area and asked, “Are you satisfied with the city’s public transit system?” Of those surveyed, $64%$ responded that they were satisfied.\n\nBased on this result, which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n1. Of all workers in the metropolitan area, exactly $64%$ are satisfied with the public transit system.\n2. If another $1,200$ workers selected at random from the area were surveyed, exactly $64%$ of them would report being satisfied.\n3. If $1,200$ workers selected at random from a different metropolitan area were surveyed, $64%$ of them would report being satisfied." 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213681 1072 #uuid "68f5d2d0-9e30-5b7f-944f-8c564163d29f" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213682 1068 #edb/ref 17592186211899 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213682 1069 "q-301338" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213682 1071 "A consumer group surveyed $800$ smartphone owners who were selected at random from a single city and asked, “Is your current smartphone less than two years old?” Of those surveyed, $60%$ responded “yes”.\n\nBased on this result, which of the following conclusions are appropriate?\n\n1. Of all smartphone owners in the city, exactly $60%$ of them have a smartphone that is less than two years old.\n2. If another $800$ smartphone owners selected at random from the city were surveyed, the proportion who say “yes” is likely to be close to $60%$.\n3. If $800$ smartphone owners selected at random from a different city were surveyed, the proportion who say “yes” is likely to be close to $60%$." 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213682 1072 #uuid "5f436633-f1eb-5cfb-9516-fc35d3980af0" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213683 1068 #edb/ref 17592186211905 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213683 1069 "q-301362" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213683 1071 "A survey was conducted using a sample of elementary school librarians randomly selected from public schools in the state of Oregon. The librarians surveyed were asked about the average number of books they check out to students each week. What is the largest population to which the results of the survey can be generalized?" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213683 1072 #uuid "7befc225-8e14-53e8-ad92-22fbecb81b1b" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213684 1068 #edb/ref 17592186211911 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213684 1069 "q-301381" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213684 1071 "A wildlife biologist is studying a population of $240$ sea turtles in a coastal bay. She randomly selects a group of turtles from the population and records whether each turtle has barnacles on its shell.\n\nWhat are the sampling units in this study?" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213684 1072 #uuid "88edfd1a-5430-56dd-a822-1adf85aedd8b" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213685 1068 #edb/ref 17592186211917 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213685 1069 "q-301383" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213685 1071 "An environmental agency is studying plant diversity in a large grassland. The grassland is divided into $500$ square plots, each measuring $10 \\cdot 10$ meters. Researchers randomly select $50$ plots and record the number of different plant species growing in each plot.\n\nWhat are the *sampling units* in this study?" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213685 1072 #uuid "64e8f8f7-65f1-554a-8539-9ccb78c05c32" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213686 1068 #edb/ref 17592186211923 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213686 1068 #edb/ref 17592186211926 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213686 1069 "q-301384" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213686 1071 "![](images/37/37dfee096050027c103829632f70a1753d6feeb5d532ede5933e0b7e0f77dc3c.png)\n\nA teacher recorded 