6213710 1071 "Given that $4(2^{x + 2}) + 2^{x} = k(2^{x})$, find the value of $k$." 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213710 1072 #uuid "edc8ef1f-c88f-5d17-a372-16d4b655c823" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213711 1068 #edb/ref 17592186212085 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213711 1069 "q-301712" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213711 1071 "Given that $4(5^{x + 1}) - 3(5^{x}) = k(5^{x})$, find the value of $k$." 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213711 1072 #uuid "33541d6f-d36e-54e4-9fe5-70c84385a740" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213712 1068 #edb/ref 17592186212091 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213712 1069 "q-301720" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213712 1071 "A financial analyst wants to estimate the average annual return of mutual funds over the past $20$ years.\n\nWhich of the following sampling methods is most likely to produce unbiased results?\n\n1. Selecting funds that are still active today and calculating their past $20$-year returns.\n2. Selecting a random set of funds from the list of all funds that existed at any point in the past $20$ years, including those that have since closed.\n3. Selecting the top-performing funds from the past five years and using their historical returns." 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213712 1072 #uuid "dd41b6dc-fa48-5b12-8c56-3efedc6ec249" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213713 1068 #edb/ref 17592186212097 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213713 1069 "q-301731" 13194139533377 17592186045585 true] [17592186213713 1071 "A town council wants to assess the opinions of all town residents about building a new community swimming pool.\n\nWhich of the following sampling methods is most likely to produce unbiased results?\n\n1. Randomly selecting a sample of residents drawn from the town’s swim-club membership list.\n2. Randomly selecting residents from a comprehensive town address registry (i